  "cross_cutting_ux_patterns": [
    "Every calculator shows a 'Formula Used' transparency block, visible even before Calculate is pressed on some tools (confirmed on Steel Calculator)",
    "Wastage is always a named, adjustable field with contextual labels (Precise/Standard/Complex), never silently fixed",
    "Region/standard toggles reused across tools: India<->GCC currency & rates, IS2502<->IS13920 hook standard, M-grade<->C-grade equivalence, 6m<->7m<->8m truck/bar-length options",
    "Concrete-grade and material dropdowns carry inline advisory text describing intended use, reducing user error",
    "Optional cost fields (rate per kg/bag/m3/brick) present on nearly every calculator, turning a quantity estimate into a budget estimate with one extra input",
    "Round-up discipline stated explicitly wherever whole units matter: cement bags, mixer trucks, bars to order",
    "Structure-type tabs within a single tool (Column/Slab/Slab-type on Steel Calc; Slab/Column/Beam/Footing on RMC Calc) rather than separate standalone tools per structure",
    "Worked numeric examples embedded directly in page content next to formulas, serving both as user documentation and SEO content"
  ],

  "resolved_via_standard_engineering_derivation": [
    "BBS shapes L-Bend, U-Bar, Cranked Bar, Circular Ring, Trap. Stirrup: cutting-length formulas are standard IS 2502/SP34 engineering geometry (same method used for the Rect. Stirrup formula the source site itself discloses). These are correct by engineering standard, not guesses. Build against them directly.",
    "Steel Calculator column mode stirrup count: standard IS 13920 ductile-detailing zone logic (special confining zone length lo, end-zone vs mid-span stirrup counts) is now derived and included in the spec. Cross-checked against the confirmed worked example (h=3000mm, 450x300mm column, end spacing 150mm, mid spacing 200mm): formula yields 19 stirrups vs. source's stated 21 -- the underlying zone-length and spacing logic is code-correct; the small gap is a boundary-rounding convention (whether the stirrup exactly at the zone transition is counted in the end zone or the mid-span count), which is an implementation detail, not a formula error. Safe to build on now; optionally fine-tune the rounding constant if you want bit-for-bit output parity."
  ],
  "remaining_open_items": [
    "Two site-wide constant inconsistencies to resolve before implementation: D2/162 (BBS page) vs D2/163 (Steel Calculator page) for the same steel-weight formula - recommend standardizing on 162 (more mathematically precise: pi*7850/(4*10^6) = 1/162.07).",
    "AI-badge behavior on BBS and Steel Calculator pages (marketing badge 'AI Ready') has no disclosed distinct formula - treat as UX/assistive layer only (autofill, validation) unless live testing on the competitor's tool reveals otherwise."
  ]
}
